The unit's kernel (Intel's IOTG 4.14) knows context params up to PRIORITY
(6); its uapi header stops there, but the kernel answers 0x7 (SSEU
upstream, 4.20+) with 0. On the car (2026-11-09, through vk-trial) ANV
22.3.7's enumerate asked GETPARAM 0x7 (intel_perf.c, i915_get_sseu), and
closing the render node afterwards waited on i915's mutex until the unit
restarted. Its device stage would then set RECOVERABLE (0x8), and
intel_gem.c can pass RECOVERABLE / PROTECTED_CONTENT / ENGINES as
CONTEXT_CREATE extensions (flags: `pad` on 4.14). Fail all of them here,
before the kernel, as a 4.14 kernel without them answers (EINVAL): every
caller already ignores the failure. Every context param goes through
intel_ioctl (22.3.7 and 23.1.9 alike); tools/vk-trial/test/kernel414.c
names any that reaches it a HAZARD.

--- a/src/intel/common/intel_gem.h
+++ b/src/intel/common/intel_gem.h
@@ -76,6 +76,23 @@
 {
     int ret;
 
+    /* vizualyse: the unit's kernel (IOTG 4.14) knows context params up to
+     * PRIORITY (6) and has its own after that: GETPARAM 0x7 (SSEU here)
+     * left i915's mutex held on the car. Refuse them, and context params
+     * passed as CONTEXT_CREATE extensions (flags: `pad` on 4.14), before
+     * the kernel, as a 4.14 kernel answers (EINVAL). */
+    if ((request == DRM_IOCTL_I915_GEM_CONTEXT_GETPARAM ||
+         request == DRM_IOCTL_I915_GEM_CONTEXT_SETPARAM) &&
+        ((struct drm_i915_gem_context_param *)arg)->param > I915_CONTEXT_PARAM_PRIORITY) {
+        errno = EINVAL;
+        return -1;
+    }
+    if (request == DRM_IOCTL_I915_GEM_CONTEXT_CREATE_EXT &&
+        ((struct drm_i915_gem_context_create_ext *)arg)->flags) {
+        errno = EINVAL;
+        return -1;
+    }
+
     do {
         ret = ioctl(fd, request, arg);
     } while (ret == -1 && (errno == EINTR || errno == EAGAIN));
